1
00:00:07,425 --> 00:00:10,735
Last time, we sorted living things into four groups.

2
00:00:10,955 --> 00:00:13,055
Today, we zoom in on one group.

3
00:00:13,275 --> 00:00:14,125
Animals!

4
00:00:14,188 --> 00:00:15,958
A frog, a bird and a fish.

5
00:00:16,068 --> 00:00:17,328
All at one pond!

6
00:00:17,398 --> 00:00:18,728
Are they one group?

7
00:00:19,151 --> 00:00:20,631
Did you lock in your answer?

8
00:00:20,871 --> 00:00:22,271
One group, or three?

9
00:00:22,521 --> 00:00:23,701
Hold on to it.

10
00:00:24,215 --> 00:00:25,775
It's You against the Buddies.

11
00:00:25,995 --> 00:00:27,275
You lock in first.

12
00:00:27,495 --> 00:00:29,225
One finger for every point.

13
00:00:29,445 --> 00:00:30,975
And a lizard is hiding.

14
00:00:31,205 --> 00:00:32,035
Find it!

15
00:00:33,360 --> 00:00:34,310
Round Zero.

16
00:00:34,530 --> 00:00:35,400
A warm-up!

17
00:00:35,670 --> 00:00:37,400
A plant makes its own food.

18
00:00:37,620 --> 00:00:38,660
Can an animal?

19
00:00:38,900 --> 00:00:39,970
One, yes.

20
00:00:40,190 --> 00:00:40,990
Two, no.

21
00:00:41,220 --> 00:00:42,630
Show me with your fingers.

22
00:00:48,102 --> 00:00:49,052
Locked in!

23
00:00:49,317 --> 00:00:50,067
Two!

24
00:00:50,344 --> 00:00:52,874
Animals are unable to make their own food.

25
00:00:53,084 --> 00:00:55,444
They depend on other living things for food.

26
00:00:55,575 --> 00:00:56,565
Two fingers?

27
00:00:56,795 --> 00:00:57,955
One finger up!

28
00:01:02,679 --> 00:01:03,599
Are you ready?

29
00:01:04,019 --> 00:01:04,779
Three!

30
00:01:05,169 --> 00:01:05,809
Two!

31
00:01:06,179 --> 00:01:06,809
One!

32
00:01:07,209 --> 00:01:07,879
Go!

33
00:01:08,377 --> 00:01:09,917
So, what is an animal?

34
00:01:10,197 --> 00:01:11,257
Look at the frog.

35
00:01:11,577 --> 00:01:12,327
A head.

36
00:01:12,617 --> 00:01:13,457
A body.

37
00:01:13,757 --> 00:01:14,667
And limbs.

38
00:01:14,947 --> 00:01:16,447
Its legs are its limbs.

39
00:01:17,109 --> 00:01:18,309
Say it with me!

40
00:01:19,021 --> 00:01:22,761
Animals are living things that usually have parts such as a head,

41
00:01:22,851 --> 00:01:24,211
a body and limbs.

42
00:01:26,343 --> 00:01:30,453
Some animals live only on land, while some live only in water.

43
00:01:30,673 --> 00:01:34,213
There are also some animals that can live both on land and

44
00:01:33,963 --> 00:01:34,763
in water.

45
00:01:35,268 --> 00:01:39,548
Animals have different outer coverings as they live in different places.

46
00:01:43,086 --> 00:01:47,696
Scientists have grouped the diversity of animals around us according to their

47
00:01:47,446 --> 00:01:49,316
similarities and differences.

48
00:01:49,451 --> 00:01:51,431
They use things we can see or measure.

49
00:01:51,651 --> 00:01:54,231
These are called observable characteristics.

50
00:01:58,452 --> 00:01:59,322
Round one.

51
00:01:59,572 --> 00:02:01,232
This frog sits on a leaf.

52
00:02:01,462 --> 00:02:02,582
Then, splash!

53
00:02:02,812 --> 00:02:03,752
It swims.

54
00:02:03,972 --> 00:02:05,342
Where can a frog live?

55
00:02:05,602 --> 00:02:07,082
One, only on land.

56
00:02:07,302 --> 00:02:08,752
Two, only in water.

57
00:02:09,012 --> 00:02:10,002
Three, both.

58
00:02:10,222 --> 00:02:11,642
Show me with your fingers.

59
00:02:17,110 --> 00:02:18,060
Locked in!

60
00:02:18,190 --> 00:02:18,970
Two!

61
00:02:19,020 --> 00:02:20,290
It swims so well.

62
00:02:20,440 --> 00:02:22,000
It must live in water.

63
00:02:22,053 --> 00:02:22,903
Three.

64
00:02:23,113 --> 00:02:25,353
I saw it on a leaf, and in the pond.

65
00:02:25,403 --> 00:02:26,123
Three!

66
00:02:26,223 --> 00:02:27,743
It hops, and it swims.

67
00:02:28,239 --> 00:02:29,229
Be the frog!

68
00:02:29,489 --> 00:02:30,459
Shrink down.

69
00:02:30,689 --> 00:02:31,559
Quietly.

70
00:02:33,947 --> 00:02:35,097
You are a frog.

71
00:02:35,447 --> 00:02:37,247
You sit on a leaf, on land.

72
00:02:37,844 --> 00:02:39,264
Your skin is moist.

73
00:02:39,584 --> 00:02:41,304
It stops you from drying out.

74
00:02:41,902 --> 00:02:42,942
Now, jump!

75
00:02:44,549 --> 00:02:45,699
You are under water.

76
00:02:46,139 --> 00:02:48,919
Your strong legs and webbed feet push you along.

77
00:02:49,438 --> 00:02:51,308
Here, you breathe through your skin.

78
00:02:52,518 --> 00:02:55,378
Back on land, you breathe with your lungs as well.

79
00:02:55,971 --> 00:02:57,171
Land and water.

80
00:02:57,551 --> 00:02:58,701
Both are home.

81
00:03:01,107 --> 00:03:02,417
The answer is three.

82
00:03:02,657 --> 00:03:03,417
Both!

83
00:03:04,076 --> 00:03:05,286
Say it with me!

84
00:03:06,001 --> 00:03:10,101
Amphibians are animals that can live both on land and in water.

85
00:03:10,331 --> 00:03:12,471
Amphibians usually have four legs.

86
00:03:16,508 --> 00:03:20,168
Amphibians can breathe through their skin as well as their lungs.

87
00:03:20,302 --> 00:03:24,192
They have protective moist skin to prevent them from drying out when

88
00:03:23,942 --> 00:03:25,032
they are on land.

89
00:03:27,364 --> 00:03:29,544
Amphibians lay their eggs in water.

90
00:03:29,745 --> 00:03:32,695
Frogs, toads and salamanders are amphibians.

91
00:03:32,829 --> 00:03:34,719
So the frog is an amphibian!

92
00:03:35,932 --> 00:03:36,992
Three fingers?

93
00:03:37,212 --> 00:03:38,372
One finger up!

94
00:03:40,123 --> 00:03:40,823
My rule!

95
00:03:40,573 --> 00:03:42,503
If it swims, it is a fish.

96
00:03:42,573 --> 00:03:43,733
A frog swims.

97
00:03:43,793 --> 00:03:44,893
A duck swims.

98
00:03:44,913 --> 00:03:46,073
So they are fish!

99
00:03:46,420 --> 00:03:47,890
Something is not right.

100
00:03:48,100 --> 00:03:50,200
If you can spot it, cross your arms.

101
00:03:50,420 --> 00:03:51,330
Hold on!

102
00:03:56,837 --> 00:03:57,947
Arms crossed?

103
00:03:58,167 --> 00:03:59,307
One finger up!

104
00:03:59,537 --> 00:04:00,947
Many animals swim.

105
00:04:01,167 --> 00:04:03,777
To find the group, look at the outer covering.

106
00:04:04,210 --> 00:04:04,900
Oops.

107
00:04:05,000 --> 00:04:06,650
I must check the cover first!

108
00:04:07,227 --> 00:04:08,617
Show me your score hand!

109
00:04:08,847 --> 00:04:09,857
More than two?

110
00:04:10,087 --> 00:04:11,367
You beat the Buddies.

111
00:04:11,587 --> 00:04:12,647
Three fingers?

112
00:04:12,867 --> 00:04:13,867
High five!

113
00:04:14,664 --> 00:04:16,024
Did you spot the lizard?

114
00:04:16,284 --> 00:04:17,854
It was on the boardwalk rail.

115
00:04:18,044 --> 00:04:20,594
Does it live on land, in water, or both?

116
00:04:20,814 --> 00:04:22,084
Tell someone at home.

117
00:04:22,885 --> 00:04:25,045
Let's read today's key words together!

118
00:04:25,285 --> 00:04:26,005
Ready?

119
00:04:26,295 --> 00:04:27,405
Outer covering.

120
00:04:28,960 --> 00:04:30,820
Observable characteristics.

121
00:04:33,172 --> 00:04:34,001
Amphibians.

122
00:04:35,648 --> 00:04:36,698
Moist skin.

123
00:04:38,151 --> 00:04:39,051
Well done!

124
00:04:40,099 --> 00:04:42,079
Next: this animal has fins.

125
00:04:42,289 --> 00:04:43,919
But it hops about on the mud!

126
00:04:44,139 --> 00:04:45,959
Is it a fish, or an amphibian?

127
00:04:46,179 --> 00:04:47,659
Find out in Part Two!

128
00:04:49,424 --> 00:04:50,483
Say it with us!

129
00:04:51,283 --> 00:04:51,993
Ready?

130
00:04:52,117 --> 00:04:52,737
One!

131
00:04:53,117 --> 00:04:53,797
two!

132
00:04:54,122 --> 00:04:55,297
Now you know!
